| `secrets.scanner.exclusions` | object | `{}` | an object mapping an exact repo-relative POSIX path (normalised, no glob character, no `..` part, not absolute) to a non-empty object of rule id to a non-empty reason | `scripts/scan_secrets.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `secrets.scanner.exclusions` row | Excuses the scanner's findings of one rule in one exact file, a fixture that holds a fake credential on purpose; every other finding stays red. An exclusion the history scan did not use is exit 14, naming the path and rule; a staged scan, which sees a few files, does not judge that. A glob, a blank reason or an empty rule map is refused, naming this key. Absent, the scan writes `[using default] secrets.scanner.exclusions = {}` to stderr. | excusing a key the keyed gate judges: `tests/integration/test_committed_secrets_gate.py` has no exclusions; silencing a real credential, which must be rotated at its provider | always |
